# 1.3 GB of art source, unrelated to running the game. The shipped, runtime
# assets under public/ are what matter and they ARE tracked.
character design/
weapons/

# The Japanese environment library: 430 MB of source art, of which the game
# loads an 87 MB curated subset that IS tracked (public/assets/env/). The rest
# is six pieces too large to ship at all -- see `npm run probe:env` for the list
# and the reason, which is always uncompressed embedded textures or raw-scan
# geometry. Kept out of git on purpose: the repository already carries 740 MB of
# LFS objects against GitHub's 1 GB free storage, so a blanket `git add -A` here
# exceeds the quota and breaks LFS for everyone cloning afterwards. Force-add it
# with `git add -f "environment assets"` once there is a data pack to spend, or
# leave it -- it is art source, not something the build needs.
environment assets/

